#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fresnel_s

#% text
# `fresnel_s(z)` gives the Fresnel integral, the integral of sin(pi t^2/2) from 0 to z.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Numerical values through the error function of complex argument; odd; the limits at infinity are 1/2 and -1/2.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fresnel_s(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.43825914739035465

#% cell
fresnel_s(inf)
#% output
#= 1/2

#% cell
fresnel_s(-x)
#% output
#= -fresnel_s(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `erf`, `fresnel_s`, `fresnel_c`
